From 8d1fb09fcc0b88d6b770c58ebe9ed285937e2839 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 057/162] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali: mark the USB/DP QMP PHY
 as a mode switch

The USB3/DP combo PHY sits in the Type-C graph (pmic_glink connector ->
usb_dp_qmpphy_out) and is already an orientation switch, but without
mode-switch the PHY never registers a Type-C mux, so a DisplayPort
alternate mode entry does not reconfigure its lanes.

Add the property where the upstream "kaanapali: Enable DisplayPort"
series puts it (v2, patch 3/5 by Balaji Kalkonda, patchwork series
1186341), so that the board's DP path matches upstream before the 7.4
rebase brings the rest of that series.

[ the one line of patchwork series 1186341 v2 3/5 (Balaji Kalkonda
  <balaji.kalkonda@oss.qualcomm.com>); the rest of the series is
  already in our queue or comes with the 7.4 rebase ]
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
index 92c80e1e8503..21380d32fe0f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
@@ -3565,6 +3565,7 @@ usb_dp_qmpphy: phy@88e8000 {
 			#clock-cells = <1>;
 			#phy-cells = <1>;
 
+			mode-switch;
 			orientation-switch;
 
 			status = "disabled";
-- 
